meta {
  name: List Order Responses
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/client/orders/{{order_id}}/responses
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200 && res.body.data.length > 0) {
    bru.setVar("response_id", res.body.data[0].id);
  }
}

docs {
  # List Order Responses

  The masters who answered the auto-search and are waiting for the client to
  pick one. Only **pending** responses are listed — approved, rejected and
  superseded ones drop out, so the screen always shows live candidates.

  `master.distance_km` is the straight-line distance from that master's latest
  GPS ping to the order address, or `null` when he has never pinged. Use it to
  sort the candidate list; it is not road distance.

  `master.avatar_url` is the avatar of the account the master signed in with,
  `null` when none was uploaded. `master.rating` is the average score across all
  reviews he ever received, rounded to one decimal, `null` for a master with no
  reviews yet — show "новый мастер" rather than a zero.

  The first response id is saved into `{{response_id}}` for the Approve /
  Reject requests below.

  **Response 200:**
  ```json
  {
    "data": [
      {
        "id": 7,
        "order_id": 226,
        "status": "pending",
        "created_at": "2026-07-20T14:31:00+05:00",
        "decided_at": null,
        "rejection_reason": null,
        "master": {
          "id": 11,
          "name": "Aydogdy Ussadow",
          "phone": "+99362111222",
          "experience_years": 6,
          "distance_km": 2.4,
          "avatar_url": "http://localhost/storage/clients/11/avatar.jpg",
          "rating": 4.8
        }
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  An order nobody has answered yet returns `{ "data": [] }`.

  **Errors:**
  - `404` — order not found or does not belong to this client
  - `401` — missing / invalid token
}
